From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:41:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(repair): correct a not-fulfilled task acceptance like a
 P0/P1; owner-gate it once rounds are spent (JAM B6)

JAM B6 ("task acceptance not fulfilled: the candidate does not satisfy the
source issue") was absorbing. With a review round left, applyObservedReview
blocked the record terminally instead of returning it to work, and it
dropped the refusing receipt, so the reviewer's statement of what the issue
still requires was not kept anywhere in state. With every round spent the
record could neither merge nor be corrected, and the launcher's delivery
pass reported `delivery:<id>:spent_not_admissible` for it on every pass.

Runtime (src/, takes effect when the next runtime is installed):
- A completed review whose only refusal is a `not_fulfilled` acceptance,
  bound to the record's own issue and to its trusted live text, is a P1 (an
  unaccepted candidate never merges; only P0/P1 block). The receipt keeps
  every reviewer finding and the reviewer's acceptance verbatim. The verdict
  is normalized into one leading unresolved P1 finding
  (`task-acceptance-not-fulfilled`): the reviewer's acceptance evidence,
  bounded to the 2,000-character correction-finding bound
  (src/repair/acceptance-correction.ts).
- The record then continues exactly as a P0/P1 verdict does. While a round
  is left it returns to `work` for the ordinary charged correction, whose
  first finding is that statement (B6a). With none left, or when the receipt
  cannot hold one more finding, it parks once with its receipt as `task
  acceptance not fulfilled and no correction can follow: owner decision
  required` (B6b). No runtime path or launcher rule re-admits that park. The
  3-round ceiling, charging, refunds and every merge gate are unchanged.
- rejectedReceipt also rejects a head whose latest completed review carries
  that P1. The missing-acceptance recovery re-reviews the same head. If the
  head's earlier change-only receipt is listed first, it made the head read
  as awaiting a CI correction. That correction's green exit returned the
  head to review, and re-observation corrected it again, without end. The
  run hit its step limit with no correction. Every other verdict keeps the
  first-listed rule, and the legacy-loss bridge is unchanged.

Launcher (ops/, correct under R80):
- Retry pass (B6a): R80 blocked some records with exactly that refusal while
  an ordinary round is left. Such a record returns to `review` with only its
  blocker cleared, on its open issue and verified-open pull request. The
  runtime re-observes the standing completed review (no new review, nothing
  charged) and corrects it. This runs only under an allowlisted
  acceptance-correction runtime at generation 81+ with its own healthy proof
  (HOSTED_AUTONOMY_ACCEPTANCE_CORRECTION_RUNTIMES). The list is empty here;
  generation 81's pin commit lists R81, and a test checks every listed tree.
  Under any other runtime the pass names each such record as
  `retry:<id>:denied:acceptance_correction_requires_runtime`, because R80
  would block the same verdict again on every pass.
- Delivery pass (B6b): the delivery pass skips two shapes on an issue it did
  not read closed, without a read: the owner-gated park, and the R80
  refusal once its ordinary rounds are spent. It names them once per pass in
  the result line as `owner_gate:task_acceptance_not_fulfilled:n=<count>:<ids>`
  (12 named, the rest counted). This replaces the per-pass
  `spent_not_admissible`. Nothing is written for them and no GitHub write
  is added. The two sets are split by the ordinary round count, and the
  runtime never writes the R80 refusal again, so no record cycles between
  them.

R80 rollback (tests run against R80's own source, ignored when shallow):
- The receipt and every snapshot parse under R80. R80's own loop and planner
  predicates start the same correction with the same first finding. R80's
  plan parser accepts the planned cell, and its consumer's rule (a completed
  review with unresolved findings binds the checked-out head) accepts it.
- The owner-gated park is idle under R80.
- R80 lists the change-only receipt first and blocks the head again, never
  with a state error.
- The launcher's re-admission is blocked again by R80, uncharged.
- Control: the same verdict stored without the P1 reaches R80's merge gate
  and returns a run-level state error on every run. That is why the receipt
  carries the P1.

Live (read-only, repair sequence 41474, 2026-10-17T21:40Z, R80 installed):
- B6a: ai.ubq.fi 576 (PR 1069, 2 rounds), 653 (PR 1014, 1) and 660 (PR
  1063, 2). They are named as awaiting the runtime from this launcher's
  first pass. They are re-admitted on the first pass after R81 is pinned
  and proven, and corrected on the runtime's next review observation and
  matrix plan.
- B6b: 611 (PR 1107), 1127 (PR 1145) and 118 (PR 1113, 22 rounds) are owner
  gated from this launcher's first pass.
- 112 and 596 carry the same spent refusal, but the owner merged their pull
  requests by hand and closed both issues, so they are not named.

Shared with other generation-81 lanes: ops/hosted-autonomy-retry-pass.ts
(#153, #154), ops/hosted-autonomy-types.ts (#154), docs/DECISIONS.md (all).

Tests: acceptance-correction (RED: blocked, then step limit; GREEN),
