 A CI fix is charged in the existing `counters.retries` (`countRetry`, also counting `attempts`) and never counts a review round: at most 3 per record, never lowered, a refunded never-submitted admission included; then the record parks with `CI fix attempts exhausted (3 of 3): ...`, which no rule re-admits. A fix also needs a review round for the fixed head, counted by the hard ceiling's own rule over the durable ledger (`reviewRoundsLeft`; CI fix charges are not `review_request` admissions and never count): fewer than 3 spent, or the one-time legacy final review of the owner's legacy class, whose ceiling is its pin + 1: every ai.ubq.fi issue record whose rounds reached three under the old review-before-CI order, by the cutoff rule above (the twelve the owner named, 595, 597, 605, 610, 618, 668, 672, 673, 680, 694, 698 and 879, the sixteen R79 parked the same way afterwards, 137, 575, 583, 602, 615, 617, 629, 633, 634, 638, 650, 678, 679, 693, 754 and 1128, and the records in flight at the install). Its open final round admits the CI fix; the fix arms it for the review. One rule under one cutoff serves every check (`legacyReviewRoundPin`, `legacyFinalRoundOpen`, `legacyFinalRoundArmed` in `src/repair/review-round-cap.ts`), and every launcher read that counts rounds takes the same cutoff: the correction planner, the flake re-run's settled read that every correction plan requires (`readCiRerunSettled`; round-2 recheck P1: read without the cutoff it settled no legacy record, so 645, 646, 657, 663 and 1140 would never have got their CI fix or final review, silently, since a record pinned at its spent count reports no drift; `tests/host/hosted-autonomy-legacy-settled_test.ts` runs the real retry pass on the 645 shape) and the conflict re-admission. So the CI fix admission, the review-round ceiling and the launcher's legacy re-admission can never disagree on who gets the final review. The hosted pre-review fix route stays closed in generation 80 (`HOSTED_PRE_REVIEW_CI_FIX